# Who reviews what on GitHub. The host-owned rows mirror the ownership table in docs/PLAN.md section 5 (last row) and
# HOST_OWNED in tools/guard/check.mjs; the gate rows are the files whose loosening is owner-reserved (PLAN section 5,
# merge policy). Agents never push, so every pull request that reaches these paths (a Dependabot bump, an outside
# contribution) asks the owner for review. App paths have no row: they belong to the agents, and the host verifies
# them through the Definition of Done in docs/AI_HARNESS.md before anything reaches main.
#
# Later rows win. Keep this list in step with HOST_OWNED when the ownership table changes.

